<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12); color: #10b981; border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">OWNERSHIP TRANSFER</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Form 29 &amp; Form 30 Verification Protocols for Interstate Forms Guide Vehicle</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Form 29, the statutory Notice of Transfer, must be filed by the vehicle owner at the originating Regional Transport Office before any interstate shipment. This form officially records the change of ownership and triggers the RTO verification process.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Alongside Form 29, the seller must submit a valid road tax clearance certificate. Indian motor vehicle laws mandate that all outstanding state taxes be settled before jurisdiction changes, preventing dual taxation and ensuring legal compliance during interstate transit.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>A sworn seller affidavit is mandatory, declaring that the vehicle is free from financial encumbrances, court attachments, or third-party claims. This document protects the buyer and validates the transfer request.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Once the origin RTO verifies Form 29 and tax clearance, it issues a No Objection Certificate alongside Form 29. These documents must accompany the vehicle during transport to the destination state.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Form 30, the Application for Transfer of Ownership, is submitted by the buyer at the destination RTO within thirty days of purchase. It formally requests the issuance of a new registration certificate under the buyer’s name.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The buyer must attach a corresponding affidavit confirming lawful purchase, accurate chassis and engine numbers, and intent to comply with the new state’s registration rules. This sworn statement safeguards against fraudulent transfers.</span></li>
